WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.970
The Aztecs built their
capital, Tenochtitlan,

2
00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:04.830
on a small island.

3
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:10.310
From 1521, Spanish conquerors built Mexico
City on the ruins of the prehispanic

4
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:11.370
city.

5
00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:16.950
Today, the Templo Mayor ruins and the
colonial cathedral share the city center.

6
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.390
Are old ruins just leftovers?

7
00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.190
Do they only tell you how old a city is?

8
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.830
What can layers like these reveal?

9
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.130
In this mission, you'll read the
marks people leave on the land,

10
00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:33.830
from farm plots built up in lake water
to a temple hand-carved in India.

11
00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:38.470
Then you'll see how attitudes to gender
and ethnicity shape the use of space,

12
00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:42.050
from Singapore's housing
blocks to the Navajo Nation.

13
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:46.600
Your mission: find out what layers
like these can reveal about a place.
